 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity:** Real-time rendering is achievable due to the feed-forward nature of the parameter prediction and efficient splatting rasterization [S1][S2, unofficial].
-*   **Memory Complexity:** Depends on the number of Gaussians and the size of the feed-forward network weights [S2, unofficial].
-*   **Strengths:** High-fidelity reconstruction, real-time animation, leverages strong SMPL priors for plausible human geometry [S1][S2, unofficial].
-*   **Limitations:** Relies on accurate SMPL pose estimation; may struggle with extreme deformations or non-humanoid subjects [S1][S2, unofficial].
-*   **When to use:** When animatable full-body human avatars are needed from video data [S1][S2, unofficial].
-*   **When not to use:** For non-human subjects or when high-fidelity texture is required without geometric constraints [S3].
+*   **Time Complexity:** Rendering is $O(N)$ where $N$ is the number of Gaussians, similar to standard 3D Gaussian Splatting. Training time depends on the complexity of the feedforward network and the number of training iterations.
+*   **Memory Complexity:** $O(N)$ for storing Gaussian parameters. The feedforward network adds a small constant memory overhead.
+*   **Measured Performance:** Not given in the sources.
+*   **Hardware:** Requires a GPU for differentiable rendering and network training.
+*   **Scaling:** Scales with the number of Gaussians and the complexity of the network.
+*   **Strengths:** Real-time animation capability, high fidelity, leverages strong geometric prior (SMPL).
+*   **Limitations:** Relies on the accuracy of the SMPL model, may struggle with extreme poses or non-human subjects.
+*   **When to use:** When animatable full-body avatars are needed from monocular video.
+*   **When not to use:** When high accuracy for non-human subjects or extreme deformations is required.
 
 ## Background
-Gaussian Avatar was introduced as a method to leverage the SMPL model as a prior to reconstruct full-body avatars [S1][S2, unofficial]. It uses pose features to predict Gaussian parameters through a feed-forward network [S1][S2, unofficial]. It is part of the broader family of learning and training methods for splatting, building on [Splatting](23-splatting.md) by treating volumetric data as parametric primitives transformed and rasterized [S1][S2, unofficial].
+Gaussian Avatar was introduced as a method to leverage the SMPL model as a prior to reconstruct full-body avatars [S1][S2, unofficial]. It uses pose features to predict Gaussian parameters through a feedforward network [S1][S2, unofficial]. This approach builds on the principles of [SMPL-based rigid/non-rigid deformation](8385-smpl-based-rigid-non-rigid-deformation.md) and [3D Gaussian Splatting](52-name.md).
 
